'''Plop Dribble's'''<ref name="Trivia">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/brothers-trivia-gallery|text="Brothers" Trivia Gallery}} {{C|Slide 6}}</ref> was a [[spaceport]] [[restaurant]] at the [[Stobar Spaceport]] during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="Brothers" /> Another Plop Dribble's was located at [[the wharf]] on the planet [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Gone">{{TCW|Gone with a Trace}}</ref> During the [[Galactic Civil War]], a third Plop Dribble's restaurant could be found at [[Havoc Outpost]].<ref name="Sisters" /> While the restaurants at [[Stobar]]<ref name="Brothers" /> and Coruscant featured an all [[Aurebesh]] logo,<ref name="Gone" /> the one at Havoc Outpost featured a similar design, but was partially written in [[Outer Rim Basic]].<ref name="Sisters" />

==History==
[[File:Plop_Dribbles_Stobar.png|thumb||280px|left|Savage Opress in Plop Dribble's at Stobar, featuring the regular Aurebesh logo]]Plop Dribble's at [[Stobar Spaceport]] was visited by [[Savage Opress]] on his search for his brother, [[Maul]]. During his visit, Opress assaulted one of the waitresses, [[Sassi]], drawing the attention of local authorities. A chef working there, [[Loubo]], attempted to intervene, but was stopped as Opress threw the waitress at him.<ref name="Brothers" />

Soon after, [[Jedi]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] and his [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] visited the establishment and witnessed the aftermath of the events that had just transpired. Curious, the two wondered what happened. Loubo told them that confrontations of that sort often happened, and that he would give them a free meal.<ref name="Brothers" />

Later, Tano and [[Trace Martez]] met up with Martez's sister [[Rafa Martez|Rafa]] at [[the wharf]], a part of [[Level 1313]] on [[Coruscant]]. The two had dinner at [[Ronto Grill]], a [[restaurant]] located in the same building as another Plop Dribble's.<ref name="Gone" />

During the [[Galactic Civil War]], [[Sabine Wren]], [[Ketsu Onyo]], and [[C1-10P|Chopper]] arrived at [[Havoc Outpost]] to deliver [[EG-86]] into safe custody. Among the many signs displayed at the station was one for Plop Dribble's.<ref name="Sisters" /> A piece of [[graffiti]] in [[LothalNet comm tower E-272|Ezra's tower]] on [[Lothal]] featured the same Plop Dribble's logo as the one at Havoc Outpost.<ref name="Spark">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Spark of Rebellion]]''</ref>

